{%- comment -%}
  The numbered section head the About board repeats four times: a `NN LABEL`
  row, then a hairline under it.

  Accepts:
    number - required, the two-digit string. Literal ('01'), not derived: these
             are the four fixed sections of the page, not a list.
    label  - required, the section name. Uppercased by the design, not by CSS —
             it comes out of a theme setting already capitalised, so a merchant
             writing "Mission" gets "Mission".

  Usage:
    {%- render 'bf-about-head', number: '01', label: section.settings.mission_label -%}

  Only the head, not the whole section — Liquid has no way to hand a block of
  markup to a snippet, and the alternative (capturing each section's row into a
  string and passing it in) buys nothing while making four readable rows of
  markup unreadable. The section element and its content stay in the caller.

  The rule DRAWS rather than rises: bf-reveal.js puts `is-concealed` /
  `is-revealed` on any element carrying `.reveal`, whatever pose the classes
  after it describe, so `about__draw` in bf-main-about.css gets the same
  preloader-aware, viewport-aware, reduced-motion-aware trigger as the rises
  without a second script to run it.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="about__head">
  <bf-reveal class="reveal reveal--rise">
    <h2 class="about__head-title">
      <span class="about__head-number" aria-hidden="true">{{ number }}</span>
      <span class="about__head-label">{{ label }}</span>
    </h2>
  </bf-reveal>

  <bf-reveal class="reveal about__draw">
    <hr class="about__rule">
  </bf-reveal>
</div>
